    <!--
      The instance's Turnstile check before a code is sent or a Google sign-in is
      exchanged (MAK-243): the moment the page is being asked, and the one failure of its
      own, which is nearly always no connection to Cloudflare from this phone. The
      server's own words cover a token it refused, as for every other refusal here.
    -->
    <string name="sign_in_checking">Checking this phone…</string>
    <string name="sign_in_challenge_failed">The check before signing in did not finish. Check your connection and try again.</string>
    <string name="sign_in_check_turned_on">This instance now checks this phone before signing in. Press the button again.</string>
    <string name="sign_in_passkey">Sign in with a passkey</string>
    <string name="sign_in_passkey_failed">That passkey did not work. Try another way in.</string>
    <string name="sign_in_google">Continue with Google</string>
    <!--
      One button for every OAuth provider that is not Google, because a phone has no
      account picker for an arbitrary one: they all end at /connect in a browser, which
      offers whatever the instance configured. Named for what it does rather than for a
      provider, so an instance enabling Discord or Microsoft needs no change here.
    -->
    <string name="sign_in_browser_social">Continue in a browser</string>
    <!--
      Separate from the generic failure because adding an account is a fix the person
      holding the phone can carry out. It suggests rather than asserts, because the
      framework reports NO_CREDENTIAL for causes that have nothing to do with the accounts
      on the device: a build whose signing certificate is not on the OAuth client (which
      is every Play-signed install until the App Signing key is registered) fails exactly
      this way on a phone with an account signed in. Telling that user a fact about their
      phone that they can see is false sends them into Settings to fix nothing.
    -->
    <string name="sign_in_google_no_account">Google had no account to offer. Check that a Google account is added in Settings, or use another way in.</string>
